#====================================================================
# E2156 - Preserve BLACS runtime, empty argument, and abort output
#====================================================================

id:                     E409
trigger_tool:           cmake|ctest|fortran|mpi|runtime
phase:                  configuration|testing|runtime
error_signature:        list sub-command APPEND requires at least two arguments|error while loading shared libraries|DONE BLACS_GRIDEXIT.*missing|BLACS.*test.*failed

severity:               3
category:               cmake, fortran, runtime, ctest, mpi
match_keywords:         BLACS, runtest.cmake, TESTSTRING, list APPEND, RUNTIMEDIR, OUTPUTDIR, $ORIGIN, MPI_Abort, FLUSH, OUTNUM
title:                  Preserve runtime location, empty arguments, and flushed output in BLACS CTest

root_cause:             The upstream harness can copy a test ELF away from its $ORIGIN RUNPATH, remove an empty CMake list argument through unquoted expansion, and lose the final Fortran marker when MPI_Abort terminates before buffered stdout is flushed.
affected_scope:         CMake and CTest MPI harnesses that relocate target executables, construct optional argument lists, or intentionally terminate ranks after writing a completion marker.
verification_cmd:       Run the complete registered CTest inventory; require 100 percent PASS, both BLACS output files to contain DONE BLACS_GRIDEXIT, and the original executable RUNPATH to remain usable.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           preserve-runtime-quote-empty-flush-before-abort
rec_description:        Execute the test binary from its original runtime directory, quote any potentially empty CMake list element, and flush the Fortran output unit immediately before the intentional MPI abort path.
rec_command:            Replace the copied executable invocation with ${RUNTIMEDIR}/${TEST_PROG}, use list(APPEND tmp "${TESTSTRING}"), and add FLUSH(OUTNUM) after the completion WRITE.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual-upstream-test-harness-repair

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      explicit-runtime-environment-with-marker-contract
fallback_description:   If the executable must be relocated, rebuild or relink it for the destination and verify the same marker and argument-vector contract without weakening abort semantics.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       file\(COPY.*TEST_PROG.*OUTPUTDIR\)
forbid_1_reason:        Copying an ELF without rebinding its relative RUNPATH can make a valid build fail only at test launch.
forbid_1_consequence:   BLACS tests fail before exercising the library.

forbid_2_pattern:       list\(APPEND\s+tmp\s+\$\{TESTSTRING\}\)
forbid_2_reason:        Unquoted empty expansion removes the required list element and changes CMake command arity.
forbid_2_consequence:   The test wrapper fails during CMake script evaluation.

forbid_3_pattern:       WRITE\(OUTNUM.*DONE BLACS_GRIDEXIT.*CALL MPI_ABORT
forbid_3_reason:        A completion write without an intervening flush is not durable across MPI_Abort.
forbid_3_consequence:   The outer harness can report a false missing-marker failure.

principles:             P012
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E2156-draft-2301.md
last_updated:           2026-08-19
source_event:           ScaLAPACK 2.2.3 r10 completed 100/100 upstream CTest entries after the BLACS harness repairs.

